From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Reinsmidt <735251+ericreinsmidt@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] brick-pad says what it is: the Brick's buttons as keys with the
 GKD Pixel 2's codes, as they have been since patch 0039, not a gamepad, in
 its description, its Kconfig help and its comment. The input device keeps
 its name, Brick Gamepad, which TortOS and Diatom find it by

---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/Kconfig
@@ -335,7 +335,8 @@
 	depends on GPIOLIB && ARCH_SUNXI
 	help
 	  Say Y or M here for the TrimUI Brick's buttons, d-pad and
-	  triggers as a gamepad, read from their pins.
+	  triggers, read from their pins, as keys with the GKD Pixel 2's
+	  codes.
 
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the
 	  module will be called brick-pad.
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/brick-pad.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/brick-pad.c
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /*
- * The TrimUI Brick's buttons as a gamepad. TrimUI's own system reads them
+ * The TrimUI Brick's buttons, as keys. The Brick's original system reads them
  * from userspace, from the pin registers, so its device tree has nothing for
  * them; this reads the same 19 pins every 10 ms, the volume keys among them.
  *
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@
  * the d-pad as BTN_DPAD_*, L2 and R2 as BTN_TL2 and BTN_TR2. Menu and the two
  * front keys, which the Pixel doesn't have, are BTN_MODE, BTN_THUMBL and
  * BTN_THUMBR. The device tree gives the volume keys to the LRADC keyboard,
- * but on the Brick it never reports a thing, on TrimUI's kernel either: they
- * are pins.
+ * but on the Brick it never reports a thing, on the original kernel either:
+ * they are pins.
  *
  * The buttons pull the pins low; the pull-ups are set here, as no pinctrl
  * state covers these pins yet.
@@ -145,5 +145,5 @@
 
 module_init(brick_pad_init);
 module_exit(brick_pad_exit);
-MODULE_DESCRIPTION("TrimUI Brick buttons as a gamepad");
+MODULE_DESCRIPTION("TrimUI Brick buttons");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
